      "message": "**Issue in `test_get_frame_absolute_success`:** In earlier tests like `test_get_frame_shifted_layout_success`, you elegantly verify the output buffer using `zassert_mem_equal` against a pre-initialized expected array. However, in `test_get_frame_absolute_success`, you switch to asserting individual byte indices:\n\n```c\nzassert_equal(output_buffer[0], 0xAA, \"Data mismatch at index 0\");\nzassert_equal(output_buffer[1], 0xBB, \"Data mismatch at index 1\");\nzassert_equal(output_buffer[2], 0xCC, \"Data mismatch at index 2\");\n\n```\n\nThis leaves the remaining 533 bytes of the buffer unverified. If `get_frame` had a bug that copied garbage data beyond index 2, this test would still pass.\n\n**Recommendation:** Standardize your buffer verification. Create an `expected_output` array, populate the first three indices, leave the rest as `0` (which correctly mirrors the `memset` behavior of `fp_buffer`), and use `zassert_mem_equal` to verify the entire 536-byte chunk.",
